# MLflow tracking artifacts are intentionally ignored. Every time
# `python -m src.train` runs, MLflow logs a NEW model snapshot under
# mlruns/.../models/m-<hash>/ without deleting old ones -- committing this
# folder causes duplicate, ever-growing artifact folders in the repo.
# Evidence of experiment tracking is instead kept in the committed,
# human-readable reports/experiment_results.csv. Re-run `python -m src.train`
# locally at any time to regenerate mlflow.db and mlruns/ from scratch.
